# port-patches.sh: glm/series-r4 @ 84fd21445827 over glm/zig-engine-base @ 0db3e2f6652b (commits 2a16b14a4903..b42a552e7693); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
core prompt cache: a shared cut no longer joins two conversations

chatOf gave a kept state the conversation of the longest kept state its prompt
extends, shared cuts included. With the GLM recipe's shared prefixes on, a
second conversation behind the same system prompt resumed the first one's cut
and took its id, so TF_GLM_KEEP_PER_CHAT counted both conversations' turns
together and each evicted the other's (and the entry cap took the other
conversation's turn as a shorter state of the same one).

chatOf now passes over shared cuts, which every conversation resumes: a turn
kept after one starts a conversation of its own unless it extends an own
state. A pass that keeps a cut and then its own turn gives the two different
ids, so /health's kept_mix lists the cut as a conversation of one state (the
next patch's lane host keeps both in the request's conversation, as Python
0089 does).

Switch: none. Tests: two, written first and failing before the fix: the store
(begin and keep, the chatOf path) and the lane host over the fake lane backend
with the recipe's policy (per_chat 2). lane_host_reuse_test.zig's event switch
gains the .logprobs arm it lacked (the engine_api test binary did not build),
and keepalive.zig's two threaded tests, which then run for the first time,
stop their ticker in a defer and let a late tick land.

Measured on the pair (g1c/g1d, chat_id_check.py: turns A1 B1 A2 A3 B2 behind
one 7k-word system prompt, TF_GLM_KEEP_PER_CHAT=2, prompt cache on with
KV_POOL_GIB=4 and 8 GiB): the base engine's B2 resumed at the shared cut
(12,160 cached), the bug; with the fix B2 resumed its own state (13,568 cached
of B1's 13,588).

A base-engine fix, also offered alone (glm/pr-chat-id, the same bytes):
whichever lands first, the other copy is an exact duplicate.

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0016-zig-core-chat-id.patch

